WEBVTT

00:19:29.167 --> 00:19:32.768
EP: No, but I mean,
do you think that transparency,

00:19:32.792 --> 00:19:35.309
that this idea
that I have nothing to hide --

00:19:35.333 --> 00:19:38.309
You know, when somebody says to me,
"I have nothing to hide,"

00:19:38.333 --> 00:19:42.351
that doesn't elicit trust
inside of me, actually. I am sorry.

00:19:42.375 --> 00:19:44.726
Actually, I say,
"Why are you saying this to me?"

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:45.768
(Laughter)

00:19:45.792 --> 00:19:48.018
If you're saying this,
you must have something.

00:19:48.042 --> 00:19:50.851
AG: It sounds a little bit
like projection bias gone wrong.

00:19:50.875 --> 00:19:52.976
I agree with that for the record.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.184
I also think there's a power dynamic here
that's really intriguing,

00:19:56.208 --> 00:19:59.726
which is when I'm making
my calendar transparent,

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:01.768
I'm trying to assert